# The undo/redo pair pins that the CORE restores the derived signal with
# the collection it derives from: a step that banked the collection
# alone still reads "1 item left" after the undo (docs/deferred.md).
# TEXT ARRIVES BY set_text HERE, where undo.steps insists on keystrokes:
# a programmatic write leaves nothing on the field's native undo stack
# (D7), so Edit>Undo has exactly one possible answer.
expect label#0 "0 items left"
set_text entry#0 "buy milk"
click button#0
expect label#0 "1 item left"
expect entry#0 ""
expect_focused entry#0

# WinUI invokes through the item, and invoking a still-disabled one is
# the stowed-exception crash (docs/traps.md, 0xc000027b): the enablement
# expect is the synchronization, not just the assertion.
expect_menu "Edit>Undo" enabled
menu_activate "Edit>Undo"
expect label#0 "0 items left"

expect_menu "Edit>Redo" enabled
menu_activate "Edit>Redo"
expect label#0 "1 item left"

toggle checkbox#0 on
expect label#0 "0 items left"
